<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates not issued owing to strike.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates not issued owing to strike.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The private Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) did not issue daily spot rates for cotton because of thin attendance amid an opposition-called general strike in Karachi, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Association will reopen on Monday.</p>
<p>On Saturday, the KCA's official spot rate for the NIAB-78 variety closed at 2,673 rupees per maund (37.32 kg) and for the MNH-93 at 2,711.50.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
